            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A particular element (A) has one electron in its third shell. There is another element (B) with six electrons in its second shell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.218,
            0.775,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) How many electrons does A tend to give or take to become stable?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.235,
            0.484,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What kind of ion would it form?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.251,
            0.774,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) How many electrons does B tend to give or take to become stable?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.269,
            0.484,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) What kind of ion would it form?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.285,
            0.774,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) If A and B were to combine, what kind of bond would be formed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.302,
            0.73,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) What would be the formula for the compound thus formed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.322,
            0.774,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. An element X has six electrons in its outer shell and forms a diatomic molecule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.36,
            0.401,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Why would that be so?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.378,
            0.501,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What kind of bond would it form?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.394,
            0.637,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Draw the structure of the molecule it would form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.411,
            0.773,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) A certain other element Y has two electrons in its second shell. Draw the structure of the molecule that X would form with Y."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.448,
            0.775,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. You want to design a new ionic compound, where the total positive charge is 6+ and the total negative charge is 6 –. Which of the following combinations gives the correct number of ions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.502,
            0.326,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { 2   A l ^ { 3 + } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 3 Cl–"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.52,
            0.347,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) 3 "
            },
